%[text] # BC121 diaphragm modeling study: original shape against flat shape
%[text] **J.G. Vermond, JVsound**
%[text] Prepared on 2026-10-17. This script compares the Ansys Mechanical results of two models of the diaphragm in the same harmonic acoustics analysis: the original (conical) shape of the cone and a flat shape. The question is how much the shape of the diaphragm changes the loads of the horn and the rear chamber, and so the SPL of the loudspeaker system. Three quantities are compared: the averaged pressure on the front and the rear of the diaphragm, the SPL at 1 m (a microphone in the mesh) and the SPL at the microphones outside the mesh at 5 and 10 m.
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Contents"}
%[text] - pressure on the diaphragm (front and rear) due to the imposed velocity
%[text] - the SPL of the loudspeaker system, calculated with the FEA enclosure at 28.3 V RMS
%[text] - SPL at 1 m in the mesh domain
%[text] - SPL at 5 and 10 m outside the mesh domain
%[text] - summary of the differences between the shapes \
%%
%[text] ## Settings
%[text] The shapes are listed with the reference first; the differences are taken against the reference. Every folder in `Simulation\DiaphragmModelingStudy\<shape>\` holds the exports of Mechanical (in MPa): `Frequency Response Front.txt`, `Frequency Response Rear.txt` and `Frequency Response Mic1m.txt` (columns Frequency, Amplitude, Phase Angle, Real, Imaginary), and per far-field microphone `Far-field Maximum Pressure Mic<distance>m.txt` and `Far-field Phase Mic<distance>m.txt`.
shapes = ["OriginalShape" "FlatShape"]; % Reference first
shapeLabels = ["Original" "Flat"];
micDistances = [5 10]; % Far-field microphones outside the mesh in [m]
frequencyRange = [20 250]; % Range of the summary in [Hz]
studyFolder = fullfile(currentProject().RootFolder,"Simulation","DiaphragmModelingStudy");
sourceVoltage = 28.3; % RMS voltage of the amplifier in [V]
diaphragmVelocity = 1e-3; % Velocity imposed on the diaphragm in the FEA model in [m/s]
pRef = 20e-6; % Reference pressure for the SPL in [Pa]
numShape = numel(shapes);
numMic = numel(micDistances);
micNames = micDistances + " m";
splUnit = "dB re 20 " + char(181) + "Pa";
%%
%[text] ## Read the FEA results
%[text] The complex pressure is the real and the imaginary part of the export, converted from MPa to Pa. The pressure of a far-field microphone comes from `readFarField`. Both shapes must have the same frequencies, otherwise the differences cannot be taken.
readExport = @(file) readmatrix(file,FileType="text",NumHeaderLines=1);
pFront = []; pRear = []; pMeshMic = []; pFarMic = cell(1,numMic);
for s = 1:numShape
    folder = fullfile(studyFolder,shapes(s));
    front = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Frequency Response Front.txt"));
    rear = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Frequency Response Rear.txt"));
    mesh1m = readExport(fullfile(folder,"Frequency Response Mic1m.txt"));
    if s == 1
        frequency = front(:,1);
    end
    sameFrequency = @(f) numel(f) == numel(frequency) && max(abs(f(:) - frequency)) < 1e-3*max(frequency);
    assert(sameFrequency(front(:,1)) && sameFrequency(rear(:,1)) && sameFrequency(mesh1m(:,1)), ...
        "Shape %s has other frequencies than shape %s.",shapes(s),shapes(1))
    pFront(:,s) = (front(:,4) + 1i*front(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    pRear(:,s) = (rear(:,4) + 1i*rear(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    pMeshMic(:,s) = (mesh1m(:,4) + 1i*mesh1m(:,5))*1e6; %#ok<SAGROW>
    farField = readFarField(folder,"Mic" + micDistances + "m");
    for k = 1:numMic
        assert(sameFrequency(farField(k).Frequency), ...
            "Microphone %s of shape %s has other frequencies.",micNames(k),shapes(s))
        pFarMic{k}(:,s) = farField(k).Pressure.'; %#ok<SAGROW>
    end
end
disp("Shapes read: " + join(shapes,", ")) %[output:11e1e4c5]
%[text] The difference of a shape is taken against the reference (the first column), so it is zero for the reference itself. `spl` expresses a pressure as a level from the RMS value, so the amplitude divided by $ \\sqrt{2} $.
spl = @(p) 20*log10(abs(p)/sqrt(2)/pRef);
diffReference = @(x) x - x(:,1);
%%
%[text] ## Pressure on the front of the diaphragm
%[text] Magnitude of the pressure averaged over the front of the diaphragm (amplitude in Pa) for the imposed velocity, and the level difference with the reference. The front is the side that loads the horn.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:8c481d9f]
nexttile %[output:8c481d9f]
loglog(frequency,abs(pFront)), grid on %[output:8c481d9f]
ylabel("Pressure (Pa)"), legend(shapeLabels,Location="best"), title("Front of the diaphragm") %[output:8c481d9f]
nexttile %[output:8c481d9f]
semilogx(frequency,diffReference(spl(pFront))), grid on %[output:8c481d9f]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)"), title("Level difference with the original shape") %[output:8c481d9f]
%%
%[text] ## Pressure on the rear of the diaphragm
%[text] The rear radiates into the closed rear chamber, so it is expected to depend on the volume displaced by the diaphragm rather than on its shape.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:569ab14c]
nexttile %[output:569ab14c]
loglog(frequency,abs(pRear)), grid on %[output:569ab14c]
ylabel("Pressure (Pa)"), legend(shapeLabels,Location="best"), title("Rear of the diaphragm") %[output:569ab14c]
nexttile %[output:569ab14c]
semilogx(frequency,diffReference(spl(pRear))), grid on %[output:569ab14c]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)"), title("Level difference with the original shape") %[output:569ab14c]
%[text] Check on the exports: the front and the rear of the diaphragm must differ.
frontEqualsRear = max(abs(pFront - pRear),[],"all") < 1e-6*max(abs(pFront),[],"all") %[output:01fcc5bb]
%%
%[text] ## Calculate the SPL with the loudspeaker system
%[text] The SPL at a microphone is calculated per shape with an `lspsys` that has a `comp.FeaEnclosure` and the B&C 21SW152-8 as driver, driven with `sourceVoltage` (RMS). The enclosure gets the averaged pressure on the front and the rear of the diaphragm of that shape. The pressure at the microphone, in the mesh (1 m) or outside it (5 and 10 m), is the transfer of the FEA model times the volume velocity of the system.
splMesh1m = zeros(numel(frequency),numShape);
splFarMic = repmat({zeros(numel(frequency),numShape)},1,numMic);
asData = @(p) struct(Frequency=frequency.',Pressure=p.');
for s = 1:numShape
    sys = lspsys;
    sys.SourceVoltage = sourceVoltage;
    sys.Enclosure = comp.FeaEnclosure;
    sys.Enclosure.PressureFront = asData(pFront(:,s));
    sys.Enclosure.PressureRear = asData(pRear(:,s));
    sys.Enclosure.DiaphragmVelocity = diaphragmVelocity;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver = comp.Driver;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Re = 6;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Le = 2.2e-3;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qes = 0.38;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Qms = 6.4;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Fs = 32;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Sd = 1680e-4;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Vas = 200e-3;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Znom = 8;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Zmin = 7;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Pnom = 2000;
    sys.Enclosure.Driver.Xvar = 16e-3;
    sys.Frequency = sys.Enclosure.Frequency;
    sys.Enclosure.PressureFarField = asData(pMeshMic(:,s));
    res = sys.createResult;
    splMesh1m(:,s) = res.SoundPressureLevel(:);
    for k = 1:numMic
        sys.Enclosure.PressureFarField = asData(pFarMic{k}(:,s));
        res = sys.createResult;
        splFarMic{k}(:,s) = res.SoundPressureLevel(:);
    end
end
%%
%[text] ## SPL at 1 m (in the mesh domain)
%[text] The SPL at the microphone in the mesh, 1 m from the mouth of the horn, at the source voltage.
tiledlayout(2,1) %[output:316f1214]
nexttile %[output:316f1214]
semilogx(frequency,splMesh1m), grid on %[output:316f1214]
ylabel(splUnit), legend(shapeLabels,Location="best"), title("Microphone at 1 m") %[output:316f1214]
nexttile %[output:316f1214]
semilogx(frequency,diffReference(splMesh1m)), grid on %[output:316f1214]
xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)"), title("Difference with the original shape") %[output:316f1214]
%%
%[text] ## SPL at 5 and 10 m (outside the mesh domain)
%[text] The far-field microphones are calculated from the surface of the mesh domain. Top: the SPL, bottom: the difference with the original shape.
tiledlayout(2,numMic) %[output:9b4ad133]
for k = 1:numMic %[output:group:67c8750b]
    nexttile(k) %[output:9b4ad133]
    semilogx(frequency,splFarMic{k}), grid on
    ylabel(splUnit), title("Microphone at " + micNames(k))
    if k == 1
        legend(shapeLabels,Location="best")
    end
    nexttile(numMic + k)
    semilogx(frequency,diffReference(splFarMic{k})), grid on
    xlabel("Frequency (Hz)"), ylabel("Difference (dB)")
end %[output:group:67c8750b]
%%
%[text] ## Summary
%[text] Difference of the flat shape with the original shape in the range given by `frequencyRange`: the largest absolute difference and the RMS difference in dB. The pressures on the diaphragm are compared as levels.
inRange = frequency >= frequencyRange(1) & frequency <= frequencyRange(2);
quantity = ["Front of diaphragm" "Rear of diaphragm" "SPL 1 m" "SPL " + micNames]';
level = {spl(pFront), spl(pRear), splMesh1m, splFarMic{:}}; %#ok<CCAT>
maxDifference = zeros(numel(level),numShape-1);
rmsDifference = zeros(numel(level),numShape-1);
for q = 1:numel(level)
    d = diffReference(level{q});
    d = d(inRange,2:end);
    maxDifference(q,:) = max(abs(d),[],1);
    rmsDifference(q,:) = sqrt(mean(d.^2,1));
end
summary = table(quantity,maxDifference(:,1),rmsDifference(:,1), ... %[output:group:015a0fc9] %[output:8fedfdeb]
    VariableNames=["Quantity" "MaxDifference_dB" "RmsDifference_dB"]) %[output:group:015a0fc9] %[output:8fedfdeb]

